From b23827fae99eb18b3cac13c961e62e800339bccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:21:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: honour quota-wall reset deadlines per
 episode and reroute default-routed cards

A rate_limited requeue respawned every ~5 min even when the worker reported a
reset hours away (32 dead runs on one card), and on the 11-01 hub Codex wall
32 default-routed cards were held until the reset although anthropic routed.

- Durable per-card quota episode (kanban_quota_episode): exact-run receipt
  deadline (typed failure_resets_at, then 'resets in Nh Mm', ISO or epoch
  'resets at', retry-after), else exponential backoff capped at 2h.
- One read-only decision shared by guard, preview and dispatch: unpinned
  default/profile-default cards take the next eligible class route off the
  walled provider (recorded in run_route as +quota_reroute); explicit pins,
  strong and review tiers wait; a re-pin to a different known provider is
  admitted. Replaces waiting_for_quota_reset, which ignored the next route.
- Worker receipts record the concrete provider that ran (class routes).
- One quota_episode_notice + comment after 3 consecutive walls, delivered by
  the gateway and TUI notifiers; long cooldown holds file no fix cards.
- Malformed/unrepresentable deadlines are rejected; reroute/notice failures
  fall back to a hold so the reaper always finishes.
